@id n6_simon
# DRAFT
# Brother Simon at dusk, hiding at the back of the nave where he slept last night (night 6, snow). Only if the porter
# saved him on night 5 (n5_saved=simon). Frightened; he knows they'll come for him again, and he'd sooner help than wait.
# He knows the crypt passage: Thomas sent him down with candles for the ring (the crypt_candles note), and said, the
# last time, only one more. He can follow the porter or wait for him ([follow], [wait]; n6_simon_with).
# (He is the rite's last soul at Matins if the cult takes him. Nothing here says so.)
== start
(Brother Simon is crouched in the dark at the back of the nave, his hood up. He's on his feet before you can speak.)
Simon {afraid}: Porter. They're all out. I watched them go past the door in their horns, and not one of them was hurrying.
Simon {pleading}: They'll come for me again tonight. I know it. Let me help you. I can't sit here and wait for it.
-> topics

== again
(Simon is back in the dark, hugging himself, watching the door.)
Simon {afraid, look down}: Something went by while you were gone. I didn't look.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n6_simon_passage] What do you know of the crypt passage, brother? -> passage
* [if not n6_simon_with=follow] Come with me, Brother Simon. [follow] -> follow
* [if n6_simon_with=follow] Wait for me here, Brother Simon. [wait] -> wait

== passage [set n6_simon_passage] [note crypt_candles]
Simon {afraid, look down}: Thomas sent me down there with candles, twice since Michaelmas. A door in the granary closet that looks like the planks.
Simon {afraid}: Then a stair, and a long passage under the nave. Pegs on the wall with things hung on them, and a chest. I didn't look.
Simon {ashamed}: I set the candles in the ring by the altar, as I was told. More of them were lit each time.
Simon {afraid, swallow}: The last time, he said only one more now. I didn't ask him one more what.
-> topics

== follow [set n6_simon_with=follow]
(He swallows, and pushes back his hood.)
Simon {afraid}: I'll come. I know that stair in the dark. Only don't leave me anywhere alone.
-> end

== wait [set n6_simon_with=wait]
(He tries to smile, and can't.)
Simon {sad}: Here, then. I'll keep to the dark. Come back for me, porter.
-> end

== leave
Simon {pleading}: Porter? Don't be long. Please.
